      "id": "1qb9j81"
    },
    {
      "id": "5oeqouk",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. Echo"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "526ighl",
      "content": "• Echo is the repetition of sound caused by reflection of sound waves."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "zgg4m3j",
      "content": "• It is heard when sound reflects from a distant surface."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bbuhvga",
      "content": "• The minimum distance required to hear echo is about 17 meters."
    },
    {
      "id": "xqliv4r",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9. Uses of Ultrasound"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "e3cn6im",
      "content": "• Medical imaging (ultrasound scanning)"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "888l5pv",
      "content": "• Detecting cracks in metals"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "e2az4je",
      "content": "• SONAR used by ships to detect underwater objects"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "i2jp3hb",
      "content": "• Cleaning delicate electronic components"
    },
    {
      "id": "wgtm3pk",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "10. Noise Pollution"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qwtdbco",
      "content": "• Noise pollution refers to unwanted or harmful sound."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Sound cannot travel in a vacuum; speed is highest in solids, followed by liquids, and lowest in gases.",
        "For a clear echo to be heard, the time interval between the original sound and its reflection must be at least 0.1 seconds.",
        "Speed of sound increases with an increase in both temperature and humidity of the medium."
      ],
      "id": "1fsokvu"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ufi489n",
      "content": "• It can cause hearing problems and stress."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "uuznpop",
      "content": "• Sources include traffic, industrial machines and loudspeakers."
    },
    {
      "id": "17hos4v",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Important Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "j35hhuv",
      "content": "• Sound cannot travel in vacuum."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bz89ie0",
      "content": "• Human hearing range is 20 Hz to 20,000 Hz."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6cq54ve",
      "content": "• Sound waves are longitudinal waves."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wcc5vae",
      "content": "• Speed of sound in air is about 343 m/s."
    }
  ],
  "enriched": true
}